{"created": "2026-10-27T03:19:30.255435+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-27T03:19:30.688665+00:00", "id": 23681420, "conceptrecid": "23681419", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23681420", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23681419", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23681420", "metadata": {"title": "The Minimum Distance of Unshifted Spherical Fibonacci Lattices", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23681420", "publication_date": "2026-10-27", "description": "<p>For every Fibonacci number N=F_n&gt;=2, we prove that the unshifted rational spherical Fibonacci lattice has least Euclidean distance2/sqrt(N), uniquely attained by the north pole and the next point. This answers the separation question in Brauchart's contribution to Oberwolfach Report40/2012,p2438 (UnsolvedMath OWR-12012-001). The proof combines a global Lambert-map distance inequality with Zaremba's classical formula for the Fibonacci lattice figure of merit. More generally, a rational N-point Lambert lift with Zaremba index rho&gt;=N/4 has exactly this minimum; rho&gt;N/4 also gives uniqueness. The construction includes a pole and uses the exact rational Fibonacci angle; the claim does not concern the different shifted irrational Fibonacci spiral, discrepancy, or optimal packing among all point sets. The four-page written proof is accompanied by symbolic and integer regression checks and separately labelled floating-point diagnostics. This is a self-audited, unrefereed preprint prepared with AI assistance, without independent review, formal proof-assistant verification, or an absolute-priority claim.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Ferudun, Alper", "affiliation": "Mercury Software GmbH"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23681419"}}]}}, "title": "The Minimum Distance of Unshifted Spherical Fibonacci Lattices", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23681420", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23681420?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23681420", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23681420", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23681420", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681419", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23681419", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23681419", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23681419", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420:OWR-12012-001.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420:OWR-12012-001.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420:OWR-12012-001.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420:OWR-12012-001.pdf/full/%5E250,/0/default.jpg", "750": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420:OWR-12012-001.pdf/full/%5E750,/0/default.jpg", "1200": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:23681420:OWR-12012-001.pdf/full/%5E1200,/0/default.jpg"}, "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23681420/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23681420/access/grants", "access_users": "http